---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import { releaseSource } from "../../data/navigation";
---

<Docs
  title="Roles, tools & adapters"
  description="Choose the smallest extension for the job. A script can validate a reply, a role can supply reusable guidance, and a server tool can give MCP clients a new operation."
  toc={[
    ["function", "Wrap the public CLI"],
    ["role", "Add a role"],
    ["tool", "Add an MCP tool"],
    ["adapter", "Support another agent"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="function">Wrap the public CLI</h2>
  <p>
    Start with <a href="/extensions/ask-repo/">Build ask_repo</a> if your
    function turns application data into one question and validates the answer.
    Submit a schema 3 request on stdin and check the terminal result. Use a
    companion MCP server when an agent also needs to discover and call the
    function. The example takes both paths without a fork.
  </p>
  <h2 id="role">Add a role</h2>
  <p>
    Generate a full project manifest using{" "}
    <a href="/configuration/#project">project setup</a>. For a Codex advisory
    role named <code>editor</code>, create{" "}
    <code>.clink/prompts/editor.txt</code> with the guidance below. Add the
    displayed property to the existing top-level <code>roles</code> object in{" "}
    <code>.clink/cli_clients/codex.json</code>, preserving the rest of that full
    client definition.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="editor.txt"
    code="Prefer concrete verbs. Preserve the author’s meaning. Explain one editing choice."
  />
  <Code
    label="roles object · property to add"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        editor: {
          prompt_path: "../prompts/editor.txt",
          description: "Plain-language editing guidance",
        },
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <p>
    Bind the MCP server to the project, reconnect it, and inspect{" "}
    <code>listmodels</code> for <code>editor</code>. Call the built-in{" "}
    <code>clink</code> tool with these arguments. Role text supplements the
    tool’s instructions. The native-task profile has its own{" "}
    <code>native_task.roles</code> map. Programmatic generation receives{" "}
    <code>instructions</code> in the request.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP arguments · advisory role"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        action: "consult",
        cli_name: "codex",
        role: "editor",
        prompt:
          "Simplify this sentence: The service performs a validation of the input.",
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <h2 id="tool">Add an MCP tool</h2>
  <p>
    For a site-specific tool, the{" "}
    <a href="/extensions/ask-repo/#mcp">companion example</a> lets a host
    discover a new name through its own stdio registration. To change Clink’s
    built-in catalog, work in the Clink source checkout:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Choose a nearby implementation.{" "}
      <a href={releaseSource + "tools/challenge.py"}>challenge</a> is local,{" "}
      <a href={releaseSource + "tools/chat.py"}>chat</a> delegates, and{" "}
      <a href={releaseSource + "tools/debug.py"}>debug</a> has a caller-driven
      workflow.
    </li>
    <li>
      Define the Pydantic request, advertised input schema and tool
      implementation. Validate mandatory action or step fields in the executing
      path. Use the existing backend for delegation and propagate its errors.
    </li>
    <li>
      Expose the class in{" "}
      <a href={releaseSource + "tools/__init__.py"}>tools</a> and instantiate it
      in the <a href={releaseSource + "server.py"}>server’s TOOLS registry</a>.
      Add a named prompt template there if the tool also needs a prompt
      shortcut. A new Python prompt file alone registers neither a tool nor a
      command-line option.
    </li>
    <li>
      Exercise discovery and valid, rejected and disabled calls in an isolated
      server process. For a workflow, cover successive steps, continuations and
      external analysis disabled.{" "}
      <a href="/contributing/#checks">Run the upstream verification suite</a>.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id="adapter">Support another agent</h2>
  <p>
    A new client name can reuse an existing adapter with a complete manifest.
    Add a CLI family in source when launch flags, transport or output differ.
    Implement the family’s{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "clink/agents/"}>command adapter</a> and{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "clink/parsers/"}>response parser</a>. Provide
    fixtures for success, malformed output, errors and cancellation. Verify the
    real binary and operation-specific safety and lifecycle controls before
    enabling it. Consultation, native tasks and generation have separate
    verification and model-selection rules. See the{" "}
    <a href="/reference/#admissions">current capability table</a> and{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/cli-configuration.md"}>manifest contract</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
